 "text": "Hi, how have I been? It depends how fluent you are in both. If you speak them both at home, then regular Dutch will be easier. If you only speak English at home, then the local language is the best bet. It is. The key is practice while you still have the opportunity. In general, Dutch has sharper sounds than English, and Norwegian leans towards English. If you learn to say the Dutch r clearly, read a Norwegian book for kids. They usually have simple r and few words you don't recognize. Great. It' a lovely language. Whichever you pick, the key is practice while you live somewhere.",
